UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Page of Wands represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Spark and Experimental Inspiration''—the fresh, high-energy phase where the sovereign consciousness receives a sudden surge of creative enthusiasm, passion, or a brand-new operational vision, and begins exploring its viability without the weight of heavy expectations. Moving beyond the completed structures of previous cycles, the Page signifies the stage of ''The Enthusiastic Apprentice,'' where you purposefully open yourself to new ideas, spontaneous downloads, and raw, unpolished potential, letting your inner fire ignite entirely uninhibited by cynical calculations or past failures. Visually depicted as a young explorer standing boldly in a vast, sun-drenched desert, holding a heavy wooden staff with both hands and gazing upward at the green sprouts blooming from its tip while wearing a tunic patterned with salamanders—the ancient symbol of fire and transmutation—this archetype embodies the concept of ''Creative Discovery''—the realization that every grand enterprise begins with a single, uncorrupted spark of curiosity and a willingness to try things just to see what happens. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Idea Incubation and Initial Prototyping,'' where a fresh, lightweight script is spun up in your creative sandbox, testing the waters of a new passion and testing its potential before committing heavy enterprise assets to its development. When the Page of Wands appears, your system is registering an ''Inspiration-Peak'' status; you are being invited to stop overthinking, embrace a spirit of playful experimentation, and boldly follow the first sparks of your emergent vision.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Page of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Scattering, False Starts, or Deflated Inspiration''—a frustrating state where your creative energy is either completely gridlocked by self-doubt, fizzling out due to a lack of focus, or exploding into loud, chaotic bursts of undisciplined enthusiasm that yield absolutely no tangible output. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''chasing endless new distractions, making loud declarations, or running away from the hard work of execution'' with ''being creative and passionate,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical failure from severe energetic scattering. You are essentially ''wasting your sparks in an echo chamber of empty ideas,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''feel the immediate rush of a new project'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to ground your enthusiasm, pick a single path, and develop actual competence. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''inspired, dynamic visionary,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of frustration, creative sterility, or dynamic paralysis, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''starting a dozen things but finishing absolutely none of them,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current momentum is completely empty. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of superficial excitement and rapid burnout''; you are obsessively jumping from one distraction to another to avoid the quiet discomfort of focus, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final manifestation of your genius is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to commit to one thing and do the work, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these frantic, scattered, showy scripts, perform a brutal audit of your unfinished projects, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize silent, disciplined focus over the convenience of a loud, superficial display. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance stagnation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and completely grounded reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 25;
